<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emirate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as emirates</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An emirate is a territory ruled by an emir. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> many provinces became effectively autonomous emirates, and the Umayyad survivors in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> was organised as a federation of emirates, each governed by an emir owing allegiance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>.</p></div>
